preConditionHook:
// A SHAVED TOP MEASURED FROM THE BODY: the bar has no tail above its body, or
// at most tailTicks of one -- high is within tailTicks of maxlist(open, close).
// Mirrored, a shaved bottom: minlist(open, close) is within tailTicks of low.
//
// EL: bodyTop = maxlist(open, close); bodyBottom = minlist(open, close);
//     high - bodyTop <= tailTicks * tickSize
//
// MEASURED FROM THE BODY EDGE, NOT THE CLOSING PRICE, the whole difference
// from the existing ShavedTopBar (high - close <= shaveOffsetPoints). On a bull
// bar maxlist(open, close) IS the close and the two coincide; on a bear bar the
// body top is the *opening price*, so this rule is strictly stronger -- a bear bar
// that closed near its low but opened well under its high passes ShavedTopBar's
// short side and fails this one's long side. The merge kept the body-based and
// close-based readings apart for exactly that reason (R00-12 vs V00-46/T06-22).
//
// MinList/MaxList are ACCEPTED for tick-grid PRICE operands only
// (EL_FEATURES.md); the open and the close are raw prices, differing by exactly
// 0 or by at least one tick -- 1e9-1e11x the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance -- so
// the plain ternary stand-in is exact, the arrangement ReversalBarTailFraction
// and SmallTailsBar use. (<algorithm> is not among the emitted includes, so no
// std::min/std::max.)
//
// ABSOLUTE, NOT A FRACTION. Not SmallTailsBar (both tails as a fraction of the
// bar's own range, direction-free) and not AverageUpperTailFraction (a mean over
// a window): a tick tolerance is far stricter on a wide bar and far looser on a
// one-tick bar, so the rules fire on different bars.
//
// The book's own value is 0 -- an exact touch on the tick grid, which the
// relational tolerance handles -- and tailTicks = 1 is the "or nearly shaved"
// reading to optimize.
//
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local. Every scratch value is a localVariables
// entry, never a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double
// placement. Deepest bar touched: 0.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
bodyTop = (open[0] > close[0] ? open[0] : close[0]);
bodyBottom = (open[0] < close[0] ? open[0] : close[0]);
